+# enginev2 — PathCE-first 40-year portfolio engine (versioned package)
+
+Reproducible snapshot of the EngineV2 campaign (investing Project, Addenda 1–6, 2026-08-29 → 2026-09-03):
+the Monte Carlo engine, the closed-form scenario metrics, the historical vol pipeline, the scenario
+decks with row-confidence grades, the named books, and the flexible-draw rule — plus `reproduce.py`,
+which regenerates the reference metrics from a monthly-returns panel.
+
+```
+pip install -r requirements.txt          # numpy, pandas
+python reproduce.py --check              # 11 books, 60k paths (~1 min); must print "reference reproduced to the digit"
+python reproduce.py --books R3b,R3dK --npaths 10000 --flex     # quick look with the guardrail columns
+```
+
+## What is in here
+| path | content |
+|---|---|
+| `lib_pathce.py` | engine (`run_engine`: 60k paths, seed 42, yearly Markov stay-or-redraw λ = 1/8, lognormal annual σ = vol48, fixed 3%-of-initial year-end draw, T = 40), `FastEval` (common-random-number evaluator for search), scenario-weight constructions (canonical π and robust π), closed-form metrics (RCEW40, DRB40, R3AF vs EVG11), monthly-returns panel, vol48 / Sortino diagnostics, expense-ratio table |
+| `core.py` | 102-ticker universe, class lists and constraint set (long-only, ETF cap 15%, singles 5%/20%, semis ≤ 12%, defense ≤ 35%, nuclear/power ≤ 35%, ballast ≥ 20%, PM-equity ≤ 10%, ≤ 14 names, 1% grid, min 2%), `feasible()`, P1 floors and gates |
+| `flexdraw.py` | guardrail rule: draw 3% of initial; below 0.80× initial cut to 2.25%; restore at ≥ 1.0× |
+| `books.json` | P1, P2, R2_final, R2d, R1b_final, R1c, R3b (return book), R3d, R3dK (survival book), SP500, 60/40 |
+| `data/decks/` | `Deck_Recal_R6/R7cand/R8cand` (40-year CAGR by ticker × 24 scenarios, percent), `scenarios_24_R6` (weights, severities), `scenarios_20_canonical`, `Row_Grades_*` (A/B/C row confidence; C rows are haircut 25% toward the column median in the stress deck), `ER_R8.json` (expense ratios for the R8 additions) |
+| `data/panel/monthly_returns_canonical_20260821.csv` | the monthly total-return panel behind every reference number (month-end Adj_Close from the Project's price snapshot, 2014-01 … 2026-08; rows for 55 canonical tickers end 2026-08-21) |
+| `reference/` | the metrics tables the package must reproduce, plus the R8 marginal tests, ballast ladder, row audit and flex-draw experiments |
+
+## Reproduction contract
+`reproduce.py` with the default (canonical) panel and 60k paths reproduces `reference/R8_Books_Metrics_20260903.csv`
+to the digit (`--check`). The rng stream convention matters: robust G and L share one `default_rng(42)` stream, canonical
+G and L use a fresh `default_rng(42)`; `FastEval` (seed 777, 14k paths) is for search only and is not digit-comparable.
+
+The C-haircut anchor is the column median over this package's 102-name universe; the Addendum 6 table was run on the
+92-name R8 universe, so its `geo_Chaircut` is 0.01 lower for R3b/R3d/R3dK (12.08/11.38/11.51 there, 12.09/11.39/11.52
+here). Everything else is identical.
+
+To run on live data instead of the frozen panel:
+- `ENGINEV2_PRICES=<etf-eod>/prices ENGINEV2_ASOF=2026-08-21 python reproduce.py` rebuilds the panel the house way from
+  etf-eod's daily files (month-end last observation). Tested on the run-9 files (2026-09-02 pull): vol48 moves by 0.01pp
+  on P1/R3b/R3dK because the later pull revised history (dividend re-adjustments, repair flags), and the Monte Carlo
+  columns move by ≤ 0.01 / a few ruin paths with it.
+- `ENGINEV2_PANEL=<etf-eod>/monthly_returns.csv python reproduce.py` uses etf-eod's published panel directly (column
+  names like BRK-B are normalized to BRKB). Its August 2026 month ends 08-31 rather than the snapshot's 08-21, so vol48
+  is ~0.08pp lower and geo-PathCE 0.04–0.09 higher on the books; the current month is partial, so keep `ENGINEV2_END`
+  (default 2026-08) at the last complete month. Close to, not identical with, the reference.
+
+## Provenance and caveats (short form — the Project addenda are the record)
+- Decks: R6 = recalibrated R1–R4 rows + 4 scenarios added 2026-08-31 (Deflationary Bust, USD/Reserve-Institution Crisis,
+  Broad Kinetic Conflict, AI Abundance); R7cand adds 13 proxy rows (2026-09-01); R8cand adds 27 asset-class-gap rows and
+  re-anchors VTI/SCHD (2026-09-03). New rows are model-derived (grade C): anchor-row blends scaled by empirical betas plus
+  documented overlays — judgment, not data. The C-haircut deck and the like-for-like −200bp gate exist to keep that
+  judgment from driving allocations.
+- The 48-month vol window (2022-09 … 2026-08) is a specific regime (positive bond–equity correlation); ballast rankings
+  that lean on it (KMLM over TLT in R3dK) should be re-read if that correlation flips.
+- Fixed 3% draws are the conservative reporting basis; the flexible-draw rule is the recommended policy assumption and
+  removes ~80–90% of ruin paths for ~1% of lifetime spending.
+- Expense ratios are prospectus values as of the addendum dates; re-verify before implementation.
+- Nothing here is a recommendation to trade; it is the model the campaign used, frozen so results can be re-derived.
